the US. Like, what is the reason? And
then I get the second thing, which is-

05:07:20.330 --> 05:07:23.820
... "No, no, you just haven't gone to
the right place." I've literally gone to

05:07:23.880 --> 05:07:28.320
15 of quote unquote- ... "the right
place," and all the croissants were shit.

05:07:28.420 --> 05:07:33.220
So before I leave the planet,
I have to get to the bottom of

05:07:33.280 --> 05:07:37.250
why the United States cannot make a
proper croissant. And I don't, I'm

05:07:37.260 --> 05:07:41.970
not even asking about peak French
croissants, peak Belgian croissants-

05:07:41.970 --> 05:07:45.960
... which are the best croissants in the world.
I'm just asking about the 7-Eleven croissant

05:07:46.020 --> 05:07:49.040
from Copenhagen. Is that
too much to ask for?

05:07:49.300 --> 05:07:55.500
- That's a fascinating mystery.
What, zooming out, what's

05:07:55.540 --> 05:07:59.049
your, what's your favorite... This makes me
want to know, what's your favorite meal?

05:07:59.140 --> 05:08:01.800
Like, if you, if I gave you a last
meal and were to murder you after.

05:08:02.380 --> 05:08:05.380
- It all depends whether it's lunch
or it's dinner. If it's lunch, it-

05:08:05.510 --> 05:08:08.990
- It's one meal. What's, what's... I
feel like if you're getting murdered,

05:08:10.120 --> 05:08:11.610
it doesn't really matter
if it's lunch or dinner.

05:08:11.620 --> 05:08:13.020
- Well, depends on what time of
day you're getting murdered.

05:08:13.680 --> 05:08:14.100
- Oh, I see.

05:08:14.180 --> 05:08:18.220
- If it's an afternoon
execution, I only get lunch.

05:08:18.720 --> 05:08:18.920
- Okay.

05:08:19.020 --> 05:08:28.700
- And if I get lunch, it's at Louisiana,
the museum in north of Copenhagen.

05:08:29.560 --> 05:08:34.560
I was just there with Jamie two days
ago, and we go there all the time.

05:08:35.500 --> 05:08:37.530
The museum is lovely. We
don't go for the museum.

05:08:37.630 --> 05:08:40.160
We go for the cafeteria. That
in itself sounds crazy. Like-

05:08:40.180 --> 05:08:40.520
- Yeah, it does

05:08:40.540 --> 05:08:43.810
- ... you're gonna, you're gonna drive
half an hour to go to a cafeteria.

05:08:43.860 --> 05:08:47.100
Well, it just so happens to
be, it is the best lunch

05:08:47.980 --> 05:08:50.510
I've probably ever had in my
life. The chef there is just

05:08:51.000 --> 05:08:54.840
unbelievably good, and not only is

05:08:54.880 --> 05:08:58.790
the food amazing, what's even more
amazing to my system thinking

05:08:58.880 --> 05:09:02.570
brain is that at any one time when we were
up there, I think there were probably

05:09:02.760 --> 05:09:07.600
200 people waiting for their food.
And our food was delivered in five

05:09:07.640 --> 05:09:13.240
minutes. They have a small menu, and
clearly they make it in bulk, and it's

05:09:13.360 --> 05:09:15.860
unbelievably delicious.

05:09:15.960 --> 05:09:17.540
- Just a cafeteria at a museum?

05:09:17.760 --> 05:09:21.150
- It's a cafeteria at a museum that happens to have
the best lunch I've ever had anywhere in my life.

05:09:21.150 --> 05:09:23.170
- What kind of food are we talking
about? What kind of lunch food?

05:09:23.170 --> 05:09:27.130
- It's, like, Nordic cuisine, so it's,
it's... A funny thing is the menu, when I

05:09:27.140 --> 05:09:30.982
look at it, I was like, "Do you know what?
If I saw this menu- As a kid, I'd go like,

05:09:31.042 --> 05:09:33.152
"I'm not eating here."
It's like, I don't know-

05:09:33.212 --> 05:09:33.742
- This is pretty fancy

05:09:33.742 --> 05:09:36.732
- ... root free fruit and- ... and onions-

05:09:36.751 --> 05:09:40.172
... and all sorts of healthy stuff. That sounds
disgusting. And then you sit down and eat it,

05:09:40.232 --> 05:09:46.202
and the angels sing. But it's even more
particular than that. It's the butter.

05:09:46.752 --> 05:09:50.232
The whipped butter that they have there,
the best butter anywhere in the world.

05:09:50.432 --> 05:09:52.562
- I think that has to be connected
to the croissant mystery too.

05:09:52.812 --> 05:09:56.772
- There must be some connection.
But literally- ... even in

05:09:56.832 --> 05:10:00.432
Paris, I've never had whipped
butter that tastes as

05:10:00.492 --> 05:10:04.452
delicious as the butter does at
Louisiana in Copenhagen. Literally,

05:10:04.522 --> 05:10:06.652
I would drive 30 minutes-

05:10:06.662 --> 05:10:10.192
... to have bread and butter
at the cafeteria in Louisiana.

05:10:10.452 --> 05:10:13.572
- Well, how'd you discover that? Just
one day you went to the museum and-

05:10:13.752 --> 05:10:14.932
- I think we just went to the museum-

05:10:15.212 --> 05:10:15.542
- And you tried a whole dish.

05:10:15.542 --> 05:10:17.832
- ... and we had the lunch,
and we were like...

05:10:19.012 --> 05:10:19.752
- This is weird.

05:10:20.272 --> 05:10:24.252
- This is rivaling the best tasting
restaurants- ... I've ever been to in my

05:10:24.292 --> 05:10:26.682
life, and I've gone to
Noma a couple of times and

05:10:28.332 --> 05:10:31.232
tried what there is to try,
and this is right up there.

05:10:31.752 --> 05:10:35.552
- All right. What about dinner, since you
mentioned? Is it something different

05:10:35.772 --> 05:10:36.452
that you have to think-

05:10:36.552 --> 05:10:39.352
- Well, I think there's a
lot of good options in

05:10:40.272 --> 05:10:45.152
Copenhagen, but actually I'll pick
a place in Spain. So there is

05:10:46.432 --> 05:10:50.722
this place in Marbella called
Puente Romano. It's a hotel,

05:10:51.812 --> 05:10:56.832
and down by the beach, they have this
beach restaurant with fresh seafood.

05:10:57.692 --> 05:11:00.152
Unbelievably delicious.

05:11:01.292 --> 05:11:04.992
I'm trying to remember what it's called,
but yeah, if you look it up, the beach

05:11:05.152 --> 05:11:08.072
seafood place at Puente
Romano is incredible.

05:11:08.692 --> 05:11:13.072
- How much of great food is, like, the
place and the person you're with,

05:11:14.092 --> 05:11:17.672
right? Or the, or the experience
when you first are there?

05:11:18.632 --> 05:11:21.912
- I mean, the ambiance certainly helps,
but I think my taste buds are also just-

05:11:22.132 --> 05:11:22.512
- Okay, that-

05:11:22.542 --> 05:11:23.272
- ... in tune for-

05:11:23.282 --> 05:11:23.812
- So it's legit.

05:11:23.822 --> 05:11:24.112
- ... flavors

05:11:24.122 --> 05:11:24.952
- ... it is just good food.

05:11:24.992 --> 05:11:25.852
- It's just really good food.

05:11:27.432 --> 05:11:31.332
Because for ex- that cafeteria, it
is, there's a lot of people. Like,

05:11:31.372 --> 05:11:35.232
I wouldn't rate it as like, oh my God, this
is just a place I want to sit for two hours.

05:11:35.712 --> 05:11:37.052
But the food is so delicious.

05:11:37.892 --> 05:11:41.882
- That's one of the things I'm, in traveling
across the country, I'm realizing

05:11:41.912 --> 05:11:47.532
to sample without bias, just try things.

05:11:47.822 --> 05:11:51.512
'Cause you might, I guess you might
just be surprised. Maybe I'll find your

05:11:51.572 --> 05:11:56.432
croissant. All right, we've talked
about mortality. Talked about food.

05:11:56.512 --> 05:11:58.012
- Settled end of life.

